  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Which of the following sets is equivalent to the interval $[0,\\infty )?$",
  "worked_solution": "The interval $[0,\\infty )$ consists of all positive real numbers and zero. It is therefore equivalent to ${R}_{0}^{+}.$\n\nThe other options are *not* equivalent to the interval $[0,\\infty ):$\n\n- The set $R$ includes the negative real numbers.\n\n- The set ${R}^{+}$ does not include the zero.\n\n- The set ${R}^{-}$ does not include the positive real numbers or zero.\n\n- The set ${R}_{0}^{-}$ does not include the positive real numbers.",
